The Options screen lists the pad controls.

Neverputt has no help screen, so nothing in the game says that the left stick both
aims and sets the power, or that holding Square slows both down for a fine putt. The
Options screen is the one a player opens to find out how the game works, so the
bindings go at its foot: `putt/st_all.c`'s, with the pad indices `patches/0003` sets.

--- a/putt/st_conf.c
+++ b/putt/st_conf.c
@@ -170,6 +170,15 @@
             gui_label(jd, _("Language"),  GUI_SML, 0, 0);
         }
 
+        /* The pad's controls. Neverputt has no help screen, and this is the one screen a
+           player opens to find out how the game works. The bindings are `st_all.c`'s with
+           the pad indices `patches/0003` sets. */
+        gui_space(id);
+        gui_multi(id, _("Left stick: aim left and right, set the power up and down\\"
+                        "Cross: putt    Hold Square: fine aim    Options: pause\\"
+                        "Menus: Cross selects, Circle goes back"),
+                  GUI_SML, gui_wht, gui_wht);
+
         gui_layout(id, 0, 0);
     }
 
